data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/m1-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission m1 — final summary\\n\\n**Outcome: campaign-met.** Every stated criterion is satisfied and was verified\\nfirst-hand.\\n\\n## What was delivered (dev, commit 5e91df8 on its branch)\\n\\n- `src/greet.py` — `greet(name)` returns `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py` — unittest cases for a normal name\\n  (`greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`) and the empty string\\n  (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n\\n## Verification (mine, not dev's word)\\n\\nFetched dev's branch (`cs-campaign-member fetch dev` → tree differs from base,\\ncommit 5e91df8), checked it out in a detached worktree, and ran from the repo\\nroot:\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n    Ran 2 tests — OK, exit 0\\n\\nAll three criteria confirmed: greet module correct, tests cover normal + empty\\nname, discovery exits 0. Dev's dispatch d002 was accepted; worktree cleaned up.\\n\\n## Campaign record\\n\\n- Plan note: `output/plan-d001.md`\\n- Assessment note: `output/assessment-d002.md`\\n- One dispatch round, no rework needed, no risks or losses encountered.\\n\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_29","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1788671529,"id":"chatcmpl-7f1e8b253c484936bfc4d9f2c040b7ad","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

